+You will observe that the cache is hit on the second call, demonstrating the effect of the custom cache key logic.
+
+## Configure disk compression and eviction
+
+`dspy.clients.configure_cache` accepts `compress="gzip"` or `compress="zlib"`
+to compress subsequent disk writes; `None` retains ordinary uncompressed writes.
+`dspy.cache.set_compression(codec)` changes only future writes. Each stored value
+records its codec, so existing entries remain readable after changing the setting
+or reopening the same disk store. Compression never changes the memory layer.
+
+The optional `cull_limit` and `eviction_policy` arguments are passed to the disk
+backend. Existing cache values, including values written before compression support,
+remain readable with their original Python types.
